<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Soest Feud</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1444">1444</a>–<a href="/years/1449">1449</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soest">Soest</a> Feud was a war in which the town of Soest broke from its lord, the archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a>, and placed itself under the duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a> and count of Mark. The archbishop besieged Soest in 1447 with an army including Bohemian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> but failed, and the town stayed with Cleves-Mark, weakening Cologne's hold on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westphalia">Westphalia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/soest-feud.jpg" alt="Soest Feud" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bdk at German Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grafschaft_Mark_Entwicklung.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
